📋 The 5 Main Methods
GET 👀 — "Just show me the menu"

"I wanna SEE something, don't change anything."

Fetches data. Read-only. Doesn't modify anything on the server.

GET /users/101   →  "Show me user 101's details"
POST ➕ — "Add a NEW dish to the menu"

"Create something brand new."

Creates a new resource. Every time you POST, a new thing gets added.

POST /users   →  "Create a new user" (Body: {name: "Raj"})
PUT 🔁 — "Replace the ENTIRE dish recipe"

"Overwrite/replace the whole thing with what I'm sending."

Updates a resource by completely replacing it. If you don't include a field, it might get wiped out.

PUT /users/101   →  Replaces ALL of user 101's data with new data
PATCH 🩹 — "Just change ONE ingredient"

"Update only the specific part I mention, leave the rest alone."

Partially updates a resource. Only touches the fields you send.

PATCH /users/101   →  Body: {email: "new@email.com"} 
                    (only updates email, everything else untouched)
DELETE 🗑️ — "Remove this dish from the menu"

"Get rid of this resource."

Deletes the resource.

DELETE /users/101   →  "Delete user 101"